#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:21
msgid "A cross platform solution to node's spawn and spawnSync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:24
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:26
msgid "`$ npm install cross-spawn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:29
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:31
msgid "Node has issues when using spawn on Windows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:33
msgid "It ignores [PATHEXT](https://github.com/joyent/node/issues/2318)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:34
msgid ""
"It does not support "
"[shebangs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shebang_(Unix))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:35
msgid ""
"Has problems running commands with "
"[spaces](https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/7367)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:36
msgid ""
"Has problems running commands with posix relative paths (e.g.: `./my-"
"folder/my-executable`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:37
msgid ""
"Has an [issue](https://github.com/moxystudio/node-cross-spawn/issues/82) "
"with command shims (files in `node_modules/.bin/`), where arguments with "
"quotes and parenthesis would result in [invalid syntax "
"error](https://github.com/moxystudio/node-cross-"
"spawn/blob/e77b8f22a416db46b6196767bcd35601d7e11d54/test/index.test.js#L149)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:38
msgid "No `options.shell` support on node `<v4.8`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:40
msgid ""
"All these issues are handled correctly by `cross-spawn`. There are some "
"known modules, such as [win-spawn](https://github.com/ForbesLindesay/win-"
"spawn), that try to solve this but they are either broken or provide "
"faulty escaping of shell arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:44
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:46
msgid ""
"Exactly the same way as node's "
"[`spawn`](https://nodejs.org/api/child_process.html#child_process_child_process_spawn_command_args_options)"
" or "
"[`spawnSync`](https://nodejs.org/api/child_process.html#child_process_child_process_spawnsync_command_args_options),"
" so it's a drop in replacement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:60
msgid "Caveats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:62
msgid "Using `options.shell` as an alternative to `cross-spawn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:64
msgid ""
"Starting from node `v4.8`, `spawn` has a `shell` option that allows you "
"run commands from within a shell. This new option solves the "
"[PATHEXT](https://github.com/joyent/node/issues/2318) issue but:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:67
msgid "It's not supported in node `<v4.8`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:68
msgid ""
"You must manually escape the command and arguments which is very error "
"prone, specially when passing user input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:69
msgid ""
"There are a lot of other unresolved issues from the [Why](#why) section "
"that you must take into account"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:71
msgid ""
"If you are using the `shell` option to spawn a command in a cross "
"platform way, consider using `cross-spawn` instead. You have been warned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:73
msgid "`options.shell` support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:75
msgid ""
"While `cross-spawn` adds support for `options.shell` in node `<v4.8`, all"
" of its enhancements are disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:77
msgid ""
"This mimics the Node.js behavior. More specifically, the command and its "
"arguments will not be automatically escaped nor shebang support will be "
"offered. This is by design because if you are using `options.shell` you "
"are probably targeting a specific platform anyway and you don't want "
"things to get into your way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:79
msgid "Shebangs support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:81
msgid ""
"While `cross-spawn` handles shebangs on Windows, its support is limited. "
"More specifically, it just supports `#!/usr/bin/env <program>` where "
"`<program>` must not contain any arguments.    If you would like to have "
"the shebang support improved, feel free to contribute via a pull-request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cross-spawn_README.md:84
msgid "Remember to always test your code on Windows!"
msgstr ""

